<title>RUSSIA: Russian grain harvest 53.7 mln T on Sept 9.</title>
<headline>Russian grain harvest 53.7 mln T on Sept 9.</headline>
<dateline>MOSCOW 1996-09-11</dateline>
<text>
<p>Russia had harvested 70 percent of its grain crops, excluding maize and threshed 53.7 million tonnes bunker weight as of September 9, the state statistics committee said.</p>
<p>It said that including small private farms the harvest was 58.2 million tonnes as of September 9, a rise of 4.2 million tonnes over the same period a year earlier.</p>
<p>It released the following data:</p>
<p>			    PACE OF RUSSIAN GRAIN HARVEST</p>
<p>					  AS OF SEPT 9</p>
<p>				  1996    1995	  1994</p>
<p>Cut</p>
<p> excl maize/million ha	 33.5    35.6	  32.3</p>
<p> as pct of sown area	   70	72	    65</p>
<p>Threshed   million ha			32.1    34.4	  29.4</p>
<p>  million T bunker weight     53.7    49.7	  56.1</p>
<p>  as pct of sown area	   67	70	    59</p>
<p>  as pct of cut area	    96	97	    91</p>
<p> Yield (tonnes/hectare)	  1.67    1.45	  1.91</p>
<p>--Dmitry Solovyov, Moscow Newsroom, +7095 941 8520</p>
